# CR 307.4, 712.14: a sorcery can't enter the battlefield; if one would, it stays in its previous zone. Esper Origins,
# flashed back on turn 3, exiles itself and enters transformed as Summon: Esper Maduin, its creature back face (CR 712.14a:
# put there transformed, it is judged as that face, so it enters). Ephemerate then exiles the Maduin and returns the card:
# a double-faced card put onto the battlefield enters front face up (CR 712.14), and that face, Esper Origins, is a
# sorcery, so it stays in exile, with Ephemerate (exiled by its rebound).
#
# Turn 1: Forest, Mox Emerald, Mox Jet, Mox Pearl; Esper Origins from the hand (surveil: Forest kept, Lightning Bolt
# binned). Turn 3: the flashback ({3}{G}: two Forests, Emerald and Jet; surveil keeps Llanowar Elves and Island on top),
# chapter I puts the Elves into the hand, then Ephemerate on the Maduin with Mox Pearl.

